  "prefLabel": "Ret 302.06 Optional Membership",
  "priorExpiration": "2018-10-08",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ret 302.06 Optional Membership. A member who has elected to participate in the NHRS while employed in a position that is optional pursuant to RSA 100-A:3, I(a) shall remain a member until termination from service from such position as defined in Ret 301.02(l). Elected officials and officials appointed for fixed terms, for whom membership is optional and who elect to enroll in the NHRS, shall meet the requirements of RSA 100-A:3(a)(1)-(5). For this purpose, if a person has more than one occupation, his or her “primary occupation” shall be determined based on his or her tenure in such position, the compensation paid and the work hours required.\n\nSource. #7478, eff 4-10-01; ss by #7573, eff 10-10-01, EXPIRED: 10-10-09\n\nNew. #9562, eff 10-14-09, EXPIRED: 10-14-17\n\nNew. #12511, INTERIM, eff 4-11-18, EXPIRED: 10-8-18\n\nNew. #12707, eff 1-9-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ret100-500.html"
